1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,200
For voltage: red lead in V, black in COM.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,900
The V input has high resistance. Almost no current flows.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,000
The A jack is a shunt with almost no resistance.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:22,900
Across 230 V that is a short circuit through the meter. It can cause an arc flash.

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:29,600
Check function and jacks before every measurement.

6
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:36,900
Current only in series, connected with power off, with the right CAT rating.

7
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,900
A two-second check. Every time.
